Description: Linux Electronics Engineering & Mobile Device Servicing Platform
 HybridBench is a professional Linux desktop application that unifies
 electronics engineering, board-level diagnostics, embedded systems
 development, and mobile device servicing into a single integrated platform.
 .
 Features include:
  * Hardware Abstraction Layer (USB, UART, SPI, I2C, JTAG, SWD, CAN)
  * Electronics Workspace with instrument integration
  * Mobile Device Service Workspace (Android, iOS, Qualcomm, MediaTek)
  * AI-Assisted Diagnostics and Repair Recommendations
  * Schematic Overlay System with component recognition
  * Power Analysis with boot signature matching
  * Plugin Marketplace for extensibility
  * Project Management for repair laboratories
  * Containerized vendor toolchains (Samsung, Apple, Qualcomm, MediaTek)
Installed-Size: 652
